-(Core Function: input)
-(Implements input function with optional prompt parameter)
-(Validates: Requirements 13.2, 13.5, 13.6)

-(Input function with optional prompt parameter)
-(Reads from standard input via syscall)
-(Returns string value in %r0)

@input:
    -(Check if prompt parameter was provided in %r0)
    -(If %r0 is non-zero, it contains the prompt string)
    :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r10
    :: cmp << %r0, %r10 >>
    :: je << @input_no_prompt >>
    
@input_with_prompt:
    -(Display the prompt by calling print)
    -(Save %r0 (prompt) to %r8 temporarily)
    :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r8
    :: add << %r0, %r8 >> -> %r8
    
    -(Call print with prompt in %r0)
    :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r1  -(null terminator for print)
    :: call << @print >>
    
    -(Restore and continue to read input)
    :: jump << @input_read >>
    
@input_no_prompt:
    -(No prompt provided, just read input)
    :: jump << @input_read >>
    
@input_read:
    -(Read from standard input via hardware I/O syscall)
    -(io_read syscall reads user input and returns it in %r0)
    :: syscall << io_read >> -> %r0
    
    -(Return the input string in %r0)
    :: return << %r0 >>

-(Example usage:)
-(With prompt:)
-(  :: load.const << "Enter your name: " >> -> %r0)
-(  :: call << @input >>)
-(  -(result is now in %r0))
-(Without prompt:)
-(  :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r0)
-(  :: call << @input >>)
-(  -(result is now in %r0))
